## Data Attributes & Accessibility

### data-slot Pattern

**Pattern**: Use data-slot for styling and testing hooks

```typescript
// ✅ Good: data-slot attributes
<div data-slot="item" data-name={name} data-error={hasError ? '' : undefined}>
  <div data-slot="control">...</div>
  <div data-slot="info">...</div>
  <div data-slot="content">{children}</div>
</div>

// ✅ Good: data-slot for conditional styling
<button
  data-size={size}
  className={cn('base-classes', {
    'data-[size=md]:h-9': true
  })}
>
```

**Data Attribute Conventions**:
- Use `data-slot` for component structure hooks
- Use `data-*` for component state (e.g., `data-size`, `data-error`)
- Use for CSS selectors: `[data-slot="item"]`
- Use for testing selectors
- Keep attribute values consistent

### Accessibility Patterns

**Pattern**: ARIA attributes and semantic HTML

```typescript
// ✅ Good: ARIA attributes
<button
  type="button"
  role="switch"
  aria-checked={value}
  data-checked={value}
  disabled={loading || disabled}
>
  <span aria-hidden="true">...</span>
</button>

// ✅ Good: Visually hidden labels
<Title>
  <VisuallyHidden />
</Title>
<Description>
  <VisuallyHidden />
</Description>
```

**Accessibility Conventions**:
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Add ARIA attributes when needed
- Use `VisuallyHidden` for screen reader only content
- Maintain keyboard navigation
- Ensure focus states are visible

## Children Patterns

### Children Prop Types

**Pattern**: Support ReactNode and render functions

```typescript
// ✅ Good: ReactNode children
interface ButtonProps {
  children?: ReactNode
}

// ✅ Good: Function children (render props)
interface RepeatProps {
  children: ReactNode | ((index: number) => ReactNode)
}

export const Repeat: FC<RepeatProps> = ({ count, children }) =>
  Array.from({ length: count }, (_, index) =>
    helper.isFunction(children) 
      ? (children as RepeatChildren)(index) 
      : (children as ReactNode)
  )

// ✅ Good: Render props in Form
<Field name={name}>
  {(control, meta, form) => {
    const childNode =
      typeof children === 'function'
        ? children(props, meta, form)
        : cloneElement(children as ReactElement, props)
    return childNode
  }}
</Field>
```

**Children Conventions**:
- Use `ReactNode` for standard children
- Support function children for render props
- Use `cloneElement` to inject props into children
- Check type before calling function children

